# Learn & Play's functions translated without per-access fences (tools/ws7/recomp/xlat/relaxed.py says why and how), by
# address, for what names/relaxed.list doesn't name: the list's kernels are in symbols.map where this build has them (eight of
# this file's first entries are now there by name). These are hot functions of the Wwise thread (0x1a823c0) and the note
# detection in a song (Time Profiler, 2026-11-06), and the helpers named kernels call here where the Mac has them inline (the
# FFT's butterflies, 0x106c130): the 32-bit front end relaxes a function only when what it calls is relaxed too. Each was read for
# what relaxed.py asks: a loop counted over buffers or the effect's own state (or no loop), no write to a global, no wait on
# memory, no lock prefix. 0x1a35660 (peak_limiter_follower), 0x1a35ba0 and 0x1a08300 (expander_gain) are as hot but set a
# static's guard (0x1ed2598), so they stay fenced.
0x1a05bf0   Wwise: the FFT's radix-4 butterfly (SSE), which fft_work calls; inline in the Mac's
0x1a0ab70   Wwise: scalar SSE resampler loop
0x1a05a10   Wwise: the FFT's radix-2 butterfly, which fft_work calls; inline in the Mac's
0x1a05aa0   Wwise: the FFT's fixed radix-4 butterfly (one column, stride 256), straight-line, which fft_work calls
0x1a05f90   Wwise: the FFT's fixed step for a 1024-point plan (radix 4, straight-line), which fft_work calls; inline in the Mac's
0x1a06360   Wwise: the FFT's radix-3 butterfly, which fft_work calls; inline in the Mac's
0x1a064c0   Wwise: the FFT's radix-5 butterfly, which fft_work calls; inline in the Mac's
0x1a8fa60   Wwise: one channel mixed into another with a linear gain ramp; mix_stereo_ramp calls it per channel
0x1aaade0   Wwise: inner loop of 0x1aaaf00
0x1aaaf00   Wwise: SSE transform with a fixed table, calls 0x1aaade0
0x1ab4100   Wwise: x87 filter over a buffer
0x10622d0   note detection: x87 scan of a spectrum, counted
0x13f23e0   note detection: SSE FFT pass
0x13f2d50   note detection: bit reversal and packing of the FFT's data
0x106c130   note detection: SSE cosine of four floats in xmm0, registers and constants only (dsp_analysis_window's vcosf)
